course: dictionary
lesson: 12631
title: Disobedient
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Disobedient means not doing what you are told by a parent, teacher or person in charge. It means refusing to obey. The word has two parts: dis- means not, and obedient means doing what you are told. So disobedient means not obedient.
explain: «The puppy was disobedient and ran straight out of the gate, even after Mum called him three times.» The clue is that he ran out even though he was called back. He did not do what he was told, so he was disobedient.
explain: The opposite of disobedient is obedient. «The obedient children put on their coats as soon as the bell rang.» When you read a story, ask who follows the rules and who does not. In the story of Peter Rabbit, Peter is disobedient when he goes into Mr McGregor's garden after his mother has told him not to.
fact: Disobedient is an adjective. Its forms are disobedient, more disobedient and most disobedient.
fact: «Disobedient» means not doing what you are told; refusing to obey.
fact: The start dis- often means not, as in dishonest, which means not honest.
fact: «Obedient» is the opposite: it means doing what you are told.
fact: Following safety rules matters, so a disobedient child near a busy road can be in real danger.
exercise: «The disobedient dog ran onto the road when it was told to stay.» What does disobedient mean? | Happy to see its owner | Very tired after a long walk | *Refusing to do what it was told | Good at fetching sticks
exercise: Which word is the opposite of disobedient? | curious | ancient | *obedient | noisy
exercise: The word disobedient has the part dis-. What does dis- mean here? | again | very | before | *not
test: Ravi's teacher said, «Stay in the line.» Ravi ran off to the playground. Why was Ravi disobedient? | He wanted a drink of water | He was very tired | *He did not do what he was told | He was early for the bus
test: Which phrase means the same as disobedient? | Very sleepy | Full of joy | Quite clean | *Refusing to obey
exam: Which sentence shows a disobedient child? | «Mia put her coat on as soon as Dad asked.» | «The class sang happily at assembly.» | *«Sam ignored Mum and went out in the rain without a coat after she said no.» | «Jo and Ben tidied their room together.»
